# PUC of Texas intermediate certificates (www.puc.texas.gov & friends).
#
# Why this file exists: the 2026-08-17 build (#99) failed with
# 'unable to get local issuer certificate' fetching the PUCT calendar
# RSS from the GitHub runner — the server did not send its chain to
# that client, though it does to browsers and residential clients
# (both ECC and RSA chains captured complete from Ian's machine,
# openssl s_client, 2026-08-18). sources/puct.py appends these to
# the certifi roots for its requests, so verification completes
# whether or not the server supplies the chain.
#
# Chain: leaf -> Cloudflare TLS Issuing {ECC,RSA} CA 1 ->
# SSL.com TLS Transit {ECC,RSA} CA R2 -> AAA Certificate Services
# (root, already in certifi). Earliest expiry below: Dec 2028 —
# refresh this file if PUC re-keys or that date nears.

